IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P5-section-5: when Chapter III Section 5 (Articles 40 to 49) and the Annexes V, VI, VIII and IX apply.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Status: written from the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a
-- plain-text rendering with no legal effect; nothing here is "verified against the official text".
--
-- Which provision group? Article 113 as amended dates Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 (point (c)) and Section 4 (point (b))
-- but no point dates Section 5, so the second paragraph's general date (2 August 2026) reaches Articles 40 to 49 (keel
-- fork F-113-groups, assumed, a call for a lawyer). An Annex takes the group of the Article that gives it effect
-- (Annex V with Article 47, Annex VI with Article 43, Annexes VIII and IX with Article 49): assumed, not ruled.
-- The two helpers below only fix the group; they restate no date (the dates are the keel's: aia-timeline.l4).
--
-- Article 111(2) saves operators of high-risk AI systems placed on the market before the date of application of Chapter III
-- (as amended) unless the system is significantly changed in its design. It speaks of "operators of high-risk AI systems";
-- a notified body, the Commission, a market surveillance authority and a Member State are not operators (Article 3(8)), so the
-- functions addressed to them pass the core's constants and ask the date only. The functions addressed to a provider, an
-- authorised representative, a product manufacturer or a deployer of one high-risk AI system pass that system's route,
-- placement date and design change to the keel's applicability function (fork F-P5-saving in NOTES.md).

§ `Articles 40 to 49: the provision group and the date asked`

-- Not about one AI system: the core's route and date constants, and no design change (the keel's own instruction).
@ref Art 113 second paragraph, reaching Chapter III Section 5 (keel fork F-113-groups)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

-- About one high-risk AI system: Article 111(2) may save it (the keel's gate answers FALSE; the callers answer NOTHING).
@ref Art 113 second paragraph, with Art 111(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

-- The group whose rules a high-risk AI system's provider is subject to on the same facts (Chapter III Sections 1 to 3): used only to show
-- the gap between Section 5 and Sections 1 to 3 (P5-tests-section-5-gap.l4). It is the keel's function, called with the same facts.
@ref Art 113 third paragraph point (c), with Art 111(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 40 to 49 Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

-- Seam S14: Article 2(2). For a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I,
-- only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 apply (the keel's `Art 2(2) the provision applies ...`, in aia-scope.l4). Every function of this part that is a provision of or about
-- one high-risk AI system (the operator's duties and the system's conformity steps) asks this helper first and answers JUST FALSE (a function that is not a yes or no answer: NOTHING,
-- a regulative rule: FULFILLED) where it says TRUE. It says TRUE only where the keel answers JUST FALSE, so NOTHING and JUST TRUE from the keel leave the provision to answer on its own.
-- The provision is an Article number and a paragraph (0 = the whole Article); an Annex takes the Article that gives it effect (Annex V with Article 47, Annex VI with Article 43,
-- Annex VIII with Article 49), the same assumption as the group above; none of my provisions is a lettered Article, so the letter is "". Fork F-S14-reach (assumed, not ruled) says which functions ask.
@ref Art 2(2), through the keel's aia-scope.l4 (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Article number` IS A NUMBER
      `the paragraph` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` (`Article reference` OF `the Article number`, "", `the paragraph`)
    WHEN JUST `the provision applies` THEN NOT `the provision applies`  -- JUST FALSE: the text's own no (a list closed by "only"); JUST TRUE: the provision is on the list
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE  -- the keel does not speak (a date before Chapter I applies, another route, or no Section B products)
